# Generated runtime state, written by the scheduled jobs and committed back.
#
# Marked binary so git does not attempt a line-by-line merge. Two jobs writing
# these concurrently produced conflict markers inside a JSON file and inside a
# SQLite database, neither of which is meaningfully mergeable: a half-merged
# state.json is a broken dashboard and a half-merged state.db is a corrupt one.
#
# On a conflict, take one side whole. The scheduled run is the system of
# record, so that is normally the remote.
data/state.db                     binary
dashboard/public/data/state.json  binary -diff
state_snapshot.json               binary -diff
data/cache/bars/*.parquet         binary
